module tasks.`2026-11-23-rich-app-approval-click`

task RichAppApprovalClick {
  title "test-parity red on main: rich_app_routes_composer_approval_scroll_and_focus, the approval click never runs the tool"
  verify $ make test-rich-app-input
  paths "crates/bboxy450-term", "crates/bboxy450-harness", "crates/bbt-mux"
  brief """
    Our stand: subtract before you add; report what you removed.

    ## Evidence (2026-11-23, Oracle Vesper Greywind)
    - `make test-parity` on origin/main debec2374 in `~/mydev/bbx-live-checks`: exit 2. The only failing test,
      failing both tries (39.7 s, 48.4 s): `bboxy450-term::it swarm_workdir::rich_detach::rich_app_routes_composer_approval_scroll_and_focus`,
      panic `crates/bboxy450-term/tests/swarm_workdir/rich_detach.rs:336` "rich App witness did not progress".
      That is `wait(|| marker.exists())` right after the `ui input` click on `approval_choices[0]`:
      the approval choices appeared, the click was accepted, the tool never ran.
    - Log `~/mydev/bbx-live-checks/target/ci-local.log` lines 4005-4058; retained fixture `/tmp/rich-input-8uipzd` (app.log shows
      only accepted GUI operations and an orderly stop).
    - The machine was also running one `make land` at the time; the sibling detach test passed in the same run.

    ## Do
    Find whether the click misses (stale rect/choice geometry, scroll or focus change between the read and the click),
    is dropped (approval routing), or is slow (raise the witness wait only if the evidence shows load). Cite file:line.
    Fix the cause, not the wait. Run `make test-rich-app-input` three times green, once with a parallel build running.

    ## Report from seat:01M85BYP3G36XCA24KMY5W5363

    Fixed the rich App input witness by using settled frames for wheel and approval input. Removed first-visible readiness and reuse of pre-focus geometry. The original receipt puts the click at local y 727 while the moving choice ended at y 707.3. Three final make test-rich-app-input runs exited 0 on the first attempt with bbt_mux compiling, each printing tool=approved and the original harness identity. License, commit signature and current-source formal receipt checks exited 0. The signed worktree is clean.

    ```json
    {
      "op_id": "01M85GNSGND4AR6BJXR8QPTDJF",
      "commit": "833e8a6c46e98fcbf0576a2dcb9ae87afb4b3831",
      "report": "[[reports/2026-11-23-rich-app-approval-click.den]]",
      "verify_result": {
